2026-10-26T00:00:00Z  CLAIM    T0171 (pixel-format half): AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P hardcoded while EncoderSettings::pixelFormat exists
2026-10-26T00:05:00Z  ROOT     Two hardcodes and no check. initVideoStream set videoCodecCtx_->pix_fmt = AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P for every software encoder and videoFrame_->format = AV_PIX_FMT_YUV420P, while swPixelFormat_ (the sws target) also defaulted to 420p and was only ever assigned in the HW device path. So a settings file asking for yuv422p/yuv444p/rgb24 recorded 420p and reported nothing -- a config key that is a lie in the UI.
2026-10-26T00:05:00Z  CHANGE   src/recorder/VideoRecorderFFmpeg.cpp: avPixelFormatFor(PixelFormat) is the single mapping from the settings enum to FFmpeg; the software branch uses it for the codec context; after avcodec_open2 the NEGOTIATED format (codecCtx->pix_fmt) drives swPixelFormat_ and videoFrame_->format, because sws_scale writing one layout into a frame declared as another is corruption with no error; a negotiation that differs from the request is LOG_WARNed with both names. avPixelFormatName() is a six-case switch rather than av_get_pix_fmt_name, which failed to link here ("declaration possibly missing extern C" from ld).
2026-10-26T00:05:00Z  CHANGE   src/recorder/EncoderSettings.cpp validate(): NV12/P010LE without a hardware encoder is refused (they are hardware layouts), and rgb24 with libx264/libx265 is refused with the sentence naming yuv444p as the colour-lossless path. Everything else is left to avcodec_open2, whose failure now names the requested format.
2026-10-26T00:10:00Z  VERIFY   ./build.sh --fast --tests -> exit 0.
2026-10-26T00:10:00Z  VERIFY   aggregate unit_tests -> "[suite] TestRecorder -> 0". TheChosenPixelFormatReachesTheMuxedStream encodes three frames with yuv422p through libx264 and reads the finished file's stream codecpar->format back as AV_PIX_FMT_YUV422P; impossiblePixelFormatsAreRefusedByValidation asserts both refusals and that yuv420p/yuv444p stay legal.
2026-10-26T00:10:00Z  NOT-DONE  The frame-0 half (PBO readback gating on pboAvailable_) is untouched: it is a GL path and needs a real context to observe.
